.TH V23 6
.SH NAME
v23 \- Vanadium blessing and RPC wire formats (Inferno-native)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Limbo Vanadium port does not use Google VOM.
Blessings and RPC use UTF-8 text framed by
.IR msgio (2)
.B putstring
/
.BR getstring .
.SS Blessings
.B Encodeblessings
produces:
.IP
.EX
V23BLESS1
\fInchains\fP
\fIncerts\fP
C
\fIlen\fP
\fIextension\fP
\fIlen\fP
\fIpkstr\fP
\fIncaveats\fP
\fIlen\fP
\fIcav.id\fP
\fIlen\fP
\fIcav.param\fP
…
\fIlen\fP
\fIsigstr\fP
…
.EE
.PP
Each field after a length line is exactly that many Unicode characters,
then a newline.
.I Pkstr
and
.I sigstr
are
.IR keyring-intro (2)
.B pktostr
/
.B certtostr
text and may contain embedded newlines; length-prefixing preserves them.
.PP
Certificate content for signing is a SHA1 digest over purpose
.BR B1 ,
extension,
.BR pkstr ,
each
.IB id = param
caveat, and (for non-roots) the parent chain digest.
The Keyring signature uses
.B ha=sha1
and purpose-related hashing as implemented in
.IR v23-security (2).
.SS RPC connection
After TCP connect:
.IP 1.
Client sends encoded blessings; server sends its blessings for the peer
(via
.B forpeer
or default).
.IP 2.
Each side verifies the peer’s blessings against roots (server may TOFU if ACL
contains
.BR ... ).
.IP 3.
Calls:
.IP
.EX
putstring(\fImethod\fP)
putstring(\fIarg\fP)
→ putstring("OK" or "ERR")
  putstring(\fIresult-or-diagnostic\fP)
.EE
.IP 4.
Shutdown:
.B CLOSE
method (empty arg).
